+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage with client-side WebMCP tools. No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+On browsers supporting WebMCP, the page registers tools with `document.modelContext.registerTool`, falling back to the earlier `navigator.modelContext.registerTool` API. Unsupported browsers retain the same manual controls. No browser globals are patched or polyfilled.
+
+| Tool | Input | Effect |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `get_seasonal_menu` | Optional `query` string | Returns the Seasonal Favorites shown on the page, optionally filtered by name or description. |
+| `order_drink` | `drink_id`, optional integer `quantity` (1–10; default 1) | Opens a prefilled, editable order dialog and returns `awaiting_confirmation`. |
+| `highlight_drink` | `drink_id`, optional boolean `highlighted` (default true) | Highlights and scrolls to a drink; false clears its highlight. |
+
+Drink IDs: `maple-oat-latte`, `dark-roast-espresso`, `cold-brew`. Each tool includes a description and JSON input schema, validates arguments, and returns a text content result containing JSON. Invalid requests return `isError: true` without changing the UI.
+
+Order Now, each card’s Order drink button, and the agent order tool share the same dialog. The user must select Add order to record it on the page. Orders are local to the current page session, disappear on reload, and involve no payment or submission to a café.
+
+Run `npm test` for automated Node tests of tool registration, queries, validation, order interactions, UI updates, and unsupported browsers. The tests use lightweight DOM fixtures; they do not launch a browser or server.
+
+API reference: [WebMCP specification](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/).
